        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                "word": "décrépitude",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a5b0bb88-c743-436d-ac3c-4ba6c6c0cec7",
                        "entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "décrépitudes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                        "entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Déchéance physique qui provient d’un état de vieillesse extrême."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbef43ac-0c3e-4e99-9333-66d684275d32",
                                "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                                "text": "II y a six degrés d’âges ; savoir : l’enfance proprement dite, infantia ; la seconde enfance, pueritia; l’adolescence, la virilité, la vieillesse et la décrépitude."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afa32dd0-5599-4429-96a0-354c761529e4",
                                "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                                "text": "Cependant, malgré les soins prodigieux que le seigneur don Juan Belvidéro donnait à sa personne, les jours de la décrépitude arrivèrent ; avec cet âge de douleur, vinrent les cris de l’impuissance, cris d’autant plus déchirants que plus riches étaient les souvenirs de sa bouillante jeunesse et de sa voluptueuse maturité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2eb45f7a-a3e1-40b5-8711-23bcad18c60c",
                                "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                                "text": "[…] mais, au bout de trente ans, il ne fut point rare de voir des vieillards de cent dix et cent vingt ans, ce qui est d’ordinaire l’âge de la dernière décrépitude."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb46b991-1978-4272-8855-08734dfce59b",
                                "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                                "text": "[…] ; le singe, le tigre, le lion éloignés de leur patrie et enfermés dans nos ménageries ne tardent pas à tomber dans un état de décrépitude complet et sont presque toujours enlevés par la phthisie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77446841-392d-4153-8fa6-76e9e27100f2",
                                "sense_id": "e404ba3f-95f5-3248-93b9-ca8c28e2417c",
                                "text": "Elle […] riait des plaisanteries qu'un ivrogne adressait à une très vieille et très innocente prostituée dont la décrépitude s'adornait de perles, d'opales, de brillants, de saphirs, d'émeraudes et de rubis faux."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4add1dc4-dec8-3f48-96ca-0a517a8dbc08",
                        "entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Déchéance morale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9203505-8591-467d-afb7-2de2001c3502",
                                "sense_id": "4add1dc4-dec8-3f48-96ca-0a517a8dbc08",
                                "text": "Décrépitude morale."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "30e120bf-84d7-4620-b8d6-72d4d226533a",
                        "source_entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                        "target_lang_word": "decrepitude",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "decrepitude",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                        "entry_id": "82882d5b-93e5-3100-b504-580eac0980f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being decrepit or worn out from age or long use."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b306be2a-f7dd-408b-9c83-d4167f53d5b6",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "There prevailed in his time an opinion, that the world was in its decay, and that we have had the misfortune to be produced in the decrepitude of nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78190e11-350f-4a1f-90c6-29fbdfd06a0e",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "This was the probable destination of his sister Kate. His uncle had deceived him, and might he not consign her to some miserable place where her youth and beauty would prove a far greater curse than ugliness and decrepitude?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fec3e5a-1627-4753-8659-d91972c365cc",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "Being a trifle precipitate in his entry, he trod on a bottle, and was instantly extinguished by a Japanese screen, which appeared to collapse on him out of pure decrepitude."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7a66194-78f6-46b6-8e2b-f28dd7e36be3",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "We were encircled by a ghostly decrepitude, roads that led to nowhere, canals holding pools of brilliant, stinking water, a few nat-haunted banyan trees, grotesque with old muscled trunks and bearded roots."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1c16bda-cf01-4c8a-bc68-d6864f6eb4fa",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "He recalled that when he accompanied Nixon to Peking in February, 1972, he had been struck by Mao's decrepitude and Chou's failing health."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9a634ec-df8c-4d67-9dd6-2bfeb135bc1d",
                                                "sense_id": "d03b8500-2f12-358d-83df-c8edddabce9c",
                                                "text": "Having slapped into middle age, where thoughts of one’s general infallibility are tempered by the realisation that those creaky, achy complaints are signs of certain decrepitude, I have decided to ward against further gravitational decline by hauling my saggy, sorry self to the gym."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d76c355c-0fdb-4f8e-a6ed-76aad52b953f",
                        "source_entry_id": "33dc0447-4598-392c-b685-e2633e6525b9",
                        "target_lang_word": "decay",
